@title Dispatch queue backlog
@subtitle On-call runbook for the dispatch-jobs queue
@author Dispatch Engineering

kpi Alert | 5000 | depth above this for 10 minutes
kpi Normal depth | under 400 | the usual state
kpi Database pool | 200 connections | the cap
kpi Max consumers | 40 | the most the pool supports

!!! **Never purge dispatch-jobs.** Every message is a real customer delivery.

# Symptoms

The QUEUE_DEPTH_HIGH alert fires when depth stays above 5000 for 10 minutes. Normal depth is under 400. Drivers see new jobs arrive late in the app.

# Diagnose

- Check the queue depth and consumer count with `kubectl -n dispatch get hpa dispatch-consumer`.
- Look at the oldest message age on the queue dashboard.
- Check the database connection pool, which is capped at 200 connections.

# Fix steps

1. **Scale the consumers.**
-- a) Run `kubectl -n dispatch scale deploy dispatch-consumer --replicas=24`.
-- b) Wait 5 minutes and re-check.
-- c) If depth is still rising, scale to 40, the maximum the database pool supports.
2. **Check for poison messages.**
-- a) If one message has been retried more than 10 times, go to the next sub-step.
-- b) Move it to `dispatch-dlq` with the dlq-move tool.
3. **Pause the bulk import scheduler** in the admin console. Bulk imports add up to 3000 jobs at a time.
4. **Re-enable the scheduler gradually** once depth drops under 400.

# Escalation

If depth is still above 5000 after 20 minutes, page the Dispatch Engineering lead and open an incident in #incidents.
